From: cache-audit <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:59:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] launchers: per-image JIT/compile cache with a node-local
 overlay (#270)

Key the shared cache by image and GPU arch on the batch host: a
<image>.digest sidecar if the images CI wrote one, else a hash of the
file size and the 96-byte squashfs superblock (images are updated in
place, so the path is no key). Each node seeds a fixed node-local copy
before the engine starts (Triton group files and ninja trees store
absolute paths) and publishes new entries after /health answers, then
every 30 min. Publication is staging + rename/link: first writer wins,
no overwrites, no partial entries, no cross-node locks.

--jit-cache overlay|shared|off, --jit-cache-root. The helper is stdlib
only and embedded into master.sh like the health checker.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
